This file exists so that web/dist/ is never empty.

Go's embed directive fails to build when it matches no files, so the Go
package here cannot be compiled unless dist/ has something in it. A fresh
clone has never run `npm run build`, so a placeholder is committed at
dist/.gitkeep to keep `go build ./...` working before the dashboard is built.

Vite empties dist/ on every build, which would delete that placeholder. Vite
also copies everything in this directory (public/) into dist/ afterwards — so
keeping the placeholder here as well means each build puts it back instead of
leaving a spurious deletion in `git status`.
